lue of $243, a meaningful margin of safety.","The fair-value models disagree (dispersion 71%), and the Monte Carlo range runs $183 to $325 (P10-P90), so treat the estimate as noisy.","On multiples it looks cheap against Industrials peers: P/E 15.3 vs 24.1, EV/EBITDA 9.1 vs 13.4 and P/FCF 10.9 vs 22.9 (sector median).","Against its own history it is dear: the EBIT multiple sits 7% above its 10-year median.","Earnings yields are mixed: an FCF yield of 9.2% (above the risk-free rate) and an EBIT/EV of 7.3% (vs the 8% bar).","The 4 covering analysts target $242 on average, 69% above the price."],"prof":["ROIC of 14% earns above the cost of capital of 9.2%, but the 5pp spread is short of the 7pp moat bar; returns have been steady (CV 0.23).","It runs a 30% gross margin and converts 12% of revenue into free cash flow.","Earnings quality looks solid: cash conversion of 1.87x.","ROE of 15% comes mostly from margins and asset turnover rather than leverage (2.1x equity multiplier).","It spends 1.0% of revenue on stock compensation."],"hlth":["Leverage is conservative at 1.2x net debt to EBITDA ($438.7M of cash against $1.1B of debt), with interest covered 8.4x.","No distress or manipulation flags (Altman Z 4.1, in the safe zone).","Short-term liquidity is ample (current ratio 2.66)."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 0.4% over 3 years and 4.7% over 5 years, so growth is decelerating, and it has been lumpy (year-to-year swings of 330%).","Net reinvestment is nil (capex and working capital no more than cover depreciation), so fundamental growth is near zero.","Free cash flow has compounded 10.1% a year over five years.","Forward indicators: a book-to-bill of 1.01, a backlog worth 6% of annual revenue and deferred revenue up 70%.","Capex runs only 0.7x depreciation (2.1% of sales), so the asset base is being harvested rather than grown.","Its Rule of 40 score is 16, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business."],"own":["Insiders own a modest 1.3%, and reported institutional holdings exceed 100% of shares (a sign of heavy share lending).","It returns 8.0% a year to shareholders (7.3% in buybacks and 0.8% in dividends).","The share count has shrunk 3.4% a year over five years, steadily raising each holder's stake.","It has paid a dividend for 12 consecutive years, raising it 5.1% a year over the last five."],"people":["With about 9,682 employees, each generates about $387K of revenue, in line with the Industrials median, and revenue has grown 4.1% a year across its filed history.","That works out to $48K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $2.6M (7x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores well (2/10, lower is better).","Stock compensation averages $4K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"INVEST","conv":87,"head":"Invest: trades 41% below fair value of $243; FCF margin 12.5%.","pros":["Composite 51, above the 39 line (gates 14/25)","Trades 41% below fair value of $243","FCF margin 12.5%","Net debt/EBITDA 1.2x","Altman Z in the safe zone"],"cons":[],"flags":[],"need":[],"buy_below":206.32,"vc":{"base":242.73,"base_src":"dcf","bear":182.87,"bull":325.12,"alt_median":73.36,"n_alt":3,"gap":2.3086,"dispersion":0.7087,"level":"LOW","why":["models disagree (71% dispersion)","DCF is 231% above the other models' median ($73.36)"]},"med":{"pe":24.0501,"ev_ebitda":13.39,"pfcf":22.9066,"pb":2.9489,"roic":0.0996,"gross_margin":0.2855,"fcf_margin":0.068,"div_yield":0.0143}},"mc_quantiles":[143.94,168.41,182.87,194.03,201.36,209.01,216.79,223.39,231.23,237.69,244.11,251.12,259.07,266.25,275.62,283.92,295.44,306.74,325.12,354.63,413.32],"mc_drivers":{"growth":0.631,"discount_rate":0.288,"terminal_growth":0.021,"exit_multiple":0.06},"ticker":"ENS","date":"2026-11-13"}